WEBVTT

00:02.730 --> 00:04.060
<b>Investigation Division 1</b>

00:07.060 --> 00:08.560
Clothes
unrumpled

00:07.060 --> 00:08.560
 No external
injuries

00:08.860 --> 00:10.280
There's been a fifth victim?!

00:11.530 --> 00:12.440
Yes.

00:12.440 --> 00:15.100
They're saying the MO is the same.

00:15.100 --> 00:16.740
Expand the scope 
of the investigation.

00:17.990 --> 00:18.840
Isshiki!

00:18.840 --> 00:19.770
Yes, ma'am!

00:21.850 --> 00:23.610
You can go home and sleep.

00:23.610 --> 00:24.460
What?

00:24.460 --> 00:27.290
Why? I can handle working 
through two nights in a row!

00:27.780 --> 00:29.250
I can still do this!

00:29.670 --> 00:32.210
Do not misunderstand me, Isshiki Totomaru.

00:33.230 --> 00:35.900
Someone useless hanging around
will only make this harder.

00:38.610 --> 00:40.700
Now, now, Amamiya...

00:41.770 --> 00:43.230
<b>General Affairs</b>

00:41.770 --> 00:43.230
<b>Planning</b>

00:41.770 --> 00:43.230
<b>Archives</b>

00:41.770 --> 00:43.230
<b>Processing</b>

00:43.650 --> 00:45.940
You sure have it rough, eh?

00:46.550 --> 00:49.180
If you don't show some results soon,

00:49.180 --> 00:51.650
you might get kicked out 
of Investigation Division 1.

00:51.920 --> 00:54.110
You think so too, Kiku-san?

00:54.810 --> 00:59.110
You've been fooled by a culprit
and let them get away twice, haven't you?

00:59.110 --> 00:59.990
Three times.

00:59.990 --> 01:02.430
And in going to a neighborhood
 to get statements after dark,

01:02.430 --> 01:03.760
you got the cops called on you.

01:03.760 --> 01:05.630
I was just so caught up in it.

01:06.580 --> 01:10.480
That ridiculously earnest side of you
that doesn't think about what comes next...

01:10.480 --> 01:12.290
I really like that about you.

01:13.500 --> 01:16.010
It doesn't make for a great detective, though.

01:16.010 --> 01:18.220
I can't say I'm thrilled to hear that.

01:20.060 --> 01:23.440
The citizens are terrified
with these serial murders going on,

01:23.440 --> 01:26.190
and all I can do is wait here on standby?

01:26.190 --> 01:28.300
It's so hard to just sit here.

01:28.810 --> 01:30.320
It's killing me.

01:33.760 --> 01:36.500
There are already five victims.

01:36.910 --> 01:40.410
And there haven't been any significant 
developments in the investigation.

01:40.410 --> 01:44.400
If Investigation Division 1 
is having this much trouble,

01:44.400 --> 01:48.130
then <i>he's</i> probably the only one
 who can crack this case.

01:48.130 --> 01:48.980
What?

01:49.300 --> 01:50.840
You know someone who can do it?

01:50.840 --> 01:53.320
Who is it? Who is this guy?

01:53.320 --> 01:55.510
A certain sleuth.

01:55.510 --> 01:56.800
A sleuth?

01:57.430 --> 02:00.760
Oh, he's no ordinary detective.

02:01.320 --> 02:02.300
Huh?

02:02.970 --> 02:07.480
Ron    Kamonohashi's

02:02.970 --> 02:07.480
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

02:05.910 --> 02:07.480
This is the place?

02:11.270 --> 02:13.720
<i>That's an old photo of him.</i>

02:13.720 --> 02:15.940
<i>Looks super slick, doesn't he?</i>

02:15.940 --> 02:18.560
<i>His personality's no different.</i>

02:19.490 --> 02:22.360
<i>He also manages an apartment building.</i>

02:22.360 --> 02:25.110
<i>Try stopping by there first.</i>

02:30.810 --> 02:34.250
Well, if Kiku-san thinks he's the only way...

02:43.290 --> 02:48.230
<i>If he's got this side job, does that mean 
his detective business isn't doing well?</i>

02:46.020 --> 02:46.540
<b>Building Manager</b>

02:46.910 --> 02:48.230
<b>Building Manager</b>

02:49.050 --> 02:50.520
Is this really gonna be okay?

02:52.460 --> 02:53.560
<i>Don't get your hopes up.</i>

02:54.170 --> 02:55.020
Huh?

02:55.350 --> 02:57.360
What was that?

02:57.360 --> 02:58.710
Am I hearing things?

03:05.240 --> 03:06.700
<i>Do it yourself.</i>

03:07.040 --> 03:08.160
Huh?

03:08.930 --> 03:12.880
Are you talking to me? Might you have 
me confused with someone else?

03:13.440 --> 03:15.850
I mean, I think you have the wrong person...

03:16.380 --> 03:18.930
<i>Is that the attitude you take 
when asking someone for a favor?!</i>

03:19.950 --> 03:22.810
<i>Go back to the shrine and
 try petitioning the gods again!</i>

03:22.810 --> 03:24.210
How did you know that I—

03:24.210 --> 03:26.720
<i>Just go away. I have no business with you.</i>

03:28.370 --> 03:30.380
You have no business with me?

03:31.350 --> 03:33.940
Excuse me, but I have business with you!

03:35.900 --> 03:39.260
Kiku-san of the Metropolitan 
Police Department sent me here.

03:53.850 --> 03:55.080
Kiku sent you?

03:58.050 --> 04:00.010
Who are you?!

04:00.480 --> 04:02.110
<i>You're</i> the one who came to visit <i>me</i>.

04:02.110 --> 04:05.320
S-So you're Kamonohashi Ron-san?

04:05.320 --> 04:06.080
Yeah.

04:06.080 --> 04:09.740
With that messy mop
looking like a wad of seaweed?

04:09.740 --> 04:13.240
But you were so squeaky clean in the past...

04:13.960 --> 04:16.860
Your eyes are so dead now! 
They don't reflect the light at all!

04:16.860 --> 04:18.870
Come on! Even a dead fish's eyes do that!

04:18.870 --> 04:22.610
Are you just not satisfied unless you say 
every last thing that comes into your head?

04:23.370 --> 04:24.320
I'm sorry.

04:24.320 --> 04:27.580
Honestly... Kiku's always 
meddling in my affairs.

04:27.580 --> 04:30.790
U-Um, may I ask how you and 
Kiku-san know each other?

04:34.210 --> 04:35.400
Is it dead?

04:35.400 --> 04:36.490
It's asleep.

04:36.490 --> 04:39.950
Kiku's son and I went to school together,
 so he's looked after me.

04:39.950 --> 04:42.140
Kiku sent me <i>that</i>, too.

04:42.630 --> 04:46.530
He thinks I spend every day crying, you see.

04:46.840 --> 04:48.800
Not that he's wrong...

04:50.140 --> 04:51.600
Are you all right?!

04:52.020 --> 04:54.690
Wait, the floor is covered in cushions?

04:54.690 --> 04:57.060
I call it my Floor of Indolence.

04:57.460 --> 05:01.300
It knows my daily routine
of despair and boredom.

05:07.410 --> 05:10.980
Th-This place is pretty austere, huh?

05:10.980 --> 05:13.110
I don't get TV or internet.

05:13.110 --> 05:15.370
What? What about a computer or cell phone?

05:15.370 --> 05:18.290
I've cut off all 
information from the outside.

05:18.290 --> 05:20.400
Nothing good comes from it.

05:20.400 --> 05:21.570
It doesn't?

05:21.570 --> 05:23.140
Do you see now?

05:23.140 --> 05:25.140
How wretched and withdrawn I am?

05:25.140 --> 05:26.710
Yes, I'm getting that vibe.

05:26.710 --> 05:28.590
I've hit the depths of despair.

05:28.590 --> 05:29.760
Rock bottom, you mean?

05:29.760 --> 05:31.870
But for some reason, I don't want to say it.

05:31.870 --> 05:34.640
Then... don't?

05:34.640 --> 05:37.100
<i>This guy... He's a piece of work.</i>

05:37.100 --> 05:40.310
I'm a hunk of junk, frozen in time.

05:40.310 --> 05:43.070
You should go. Give Kiku my regards.

05:43.070 --> 05:46.460
I-I can't have that! 
I came to ask you for—

05:46.460 --> 05:47.580
I refuse.

05:47.580 --> 05:49.140
I haven't asked anything yet.

05:49.140 --> 05:50.990
You're not the first.

05:51.380 --> 05:52.480
What?

05:52.480 --> 05:55.370
Kiku has sent others to be my partner.

05:55.370 --> 05:58.210
Young, brilliant officers 
only interested in promotions.

05:58.210 --> 06:00.570
He's sent a number of them my way.

06:00.570 --> 06:03.690
I turn them all away after 
knocking them down a peg, though.

06:03.690 --> 06:05.920
Seems he really wants 
to help me make a comeback,

06:06.550 --> 06:10.190
even though he knows better than 
anyone that I'm not sleuthing anymore.

06:10.190 --> 06:13.110
What? You're not a detective anymore?

06:13.110 --> 06:15.100
What, he didn't tell you?

06:15.100 --> 06:19.770
But... I came here because Kiku-san 
told me to consult you about a case.

06:21.130 --> 06:24.400
You must've heard about it, right? 
Those serial murders in the city—

06:24.400 --> 06:27.070
What the? In the city—

06:27.610 --> 06:28.870
In the—

06:29.630 --> 06:31.820
What's with you? 
I'm trying to talk, so—

06:31.820 --> 06:34.670
That's fine.
I'm trying to keep you from talking.

06:34.670 --> 06:35.740
What?

06:35.740 --> 06:38.430
I told you I'm not sleuthing, didn't I?

06:38.430 --> 06:42.750
I want absolutely nothing to do
with unsolved cases and their ilk.

06:42.750 --> 06:44.960
What does that mean?
You could at least listen.

06:44.960 --> 06:46.460
I emphatically refuse.

06:46.460 --> 06:48.920
People's lives are on the line here!

06:48.920 --> 06:50.190
Not my problem.

06:52.070 --> 06:54.140
<i>What is wrong with him?</i>

06:54.140 --> 06:57.060
<i>There's no way this guy
could deduce anything.</i>

06:59.390 --> 07:02.860
Fine. I feel bad for Kiku-san, 
but I'm not asking for your help.

07:02.860 --> 07:04.300
Yes, that's for the best.

07:04.300 --> 07:08.150
Petitioning the gods suits you better anyway.

07:08.830 --> 07:11.990
Come to think of it,
how did you know I'd been to a shrine?

07:11.990 --> 07:13.200
Simple.

07:13.660 --> 07:16.330
The pine pollen on your shoulder.

07:16.330 --> 07:18.650
Around here, the only place you'd pick that up

07:18.650 --> 07:20.910
is walking down the path at Wakana Shrine.

07:20.910 --> 07:24.130
Plus, there's the unopened can 
of coffee in your left pocket

07:24.130 --> 07:27.210
and the jangling of small change
from your right pocket.

07:27.210 --> 07:30.170
I can tell you broke a bill 
in order to offer a coin there.

07:32.110 --> 07:33.770
That's all totally correct...

07:33.770 --> 07:35.100
Incredible!

07:35.100 --> 07:38.480
As boorish and bratty as you are, 
those were amazing deductions!

07:38.480 --> 07:41.440
Saying whatever you think without hesitation

07:41.440 --> 07:43.900
is a sign of overreliance on others.

07:43.900 --> 07:47.320
Also, walking the far sides of the shrine path
is a proper bit of etiquette

07:47.320 --> 07:49.610
you must have learned growing up.

07:49.970 --> 07:53.170
I therefore presume
you were raised by your grandparents.

07:53.170 --> 07:54.380
Am I wrong?

07:56.530 --> 07:58.660
Given your carefree disposition,

07:58.660 --> 08:01.570
you're worried Investigation Division 1
might give you the boot,

08:01.570 --> 08:03.930
so you came here looking for help, right?

08:03.930 --> 08:05.050
Urk!

08:05.050 --> 08:09.070
You're right... But that's only 
30 percent of what I'm feeling.

08:09.070 --> 08:11.220
Is it really <i>only</i> 30 percent?

08:11.220 --> 08:13.010
The real mystery here is...

08:13.010 --> 08:16.500
Kiku knew I wouldn't work with 
you for reasons like that,

08:13.500 --> 08:16.500
He's just like Kiku-san said...

08:16.500 --> 08:19.530
so why would he send me
a third-rate detective like you?

08:17.030 --> 08:20.020
He really might be able to catch the culprit!

08:20.020 --> 08:23.400
You're not having an internal monologue.
You're just talking to yourself, dolt.

08:24.350 --> 08:26.940
I won't help you, so please, just leave.

08:26.940 --> 08:29.960
Please! Lend me your abilities, 
Kamonohashi Ron!

08:29.960 --> 08:30.780
I refuse.

08:30.780 --> 08:31.950
Don't say that!

08:31.950 --> 08:33.230
I refuse.

08:34.490 --> 08:37.280
<i>Now it's come to this.
Even if I have to force him...</i>

08:37.280 --> 08:40.740
It's a serial murder case 
that no one can solve!

08:40.740 --> 08:43.710
The first victim was killed nine months ago!

08:45.090 --> 08:46.040
Huh?

08:46.040 --> 08:47.710
Earplugs?!

08:47.710 --> 08:50.460
Just how warped are you?

08:50.860 --> 08:51.840
I won't stand for this!

08:51.840 --> 08:53.070
Go away.

08:53.070 --> 08:56.640
Please listen! 
It's a terribly frightening case!

08:54.370 --> 08:55.540
Stop it!

08:58.390 --> 08:59.920
It's from my boss.

08:58.870 --> 09:02.310
Don't talk about your job here!

09:01.600 --> 09:02.060
<b>Amemiya</b>

09:01.600 --> 09:02.060
Remind me

09:01.600 --> 09:02.060
Slide to answer

09:05.960 --> 09:07.720
<i>There's been a sixth victim!</i>

09:08.590 --> 09:10.140
<i>Move out ASAP, Isshiki!</i>

09:10.980 --> 09:13.100
<i>Isshiki? Isshiki Totomaru?</i>

09:13.100 --> 09:14.600
Yes, I'm here!

09:14.600 --> 09:17.550
<i>A body was discovered
in Kazahana Park in Shibuya.</i>

09:17.550 --> 09:19.790
<i>You're the closest,
so get there as fast as you can!</i>

09:19.790 --> 09:20.970
Understood.

09:22.330 --> 09:23.660
This is bad.

09:24.030 --> 09:25.630
I'm sorry! I have to go!

09:26.790 --> 09:29.110
H-Hey, what's wrong?

09:29.850 --> 09:32.300
This is why I told you I wouldn't hear it...

09:34.680 --> 09:39.890
Once I learn about a case,
I can't hold myself back any longer.

09:39.890 --> 09:41.040
What?

09:41.350 --> 09:44.190
But I can't be allowed to sleuth anymore...

09:44.190 --> 09:46.140
That's why I distanced myself.

09:46.140 --> 09:48.310
Huh? You mean you <i>want</i> to be a detective?

09:48.310 --> 09:49.770
Of course I do!

09:50.190 --> 09:54.140
Unraveling mysteries and solving cases 
is what gives meaning to my life.

09:54.140 --> 09:57.220
Not being able to makes me 
feel like I'm going to go insane.

09:57.220 --> 09:59.900
That's why you said you're 
in the depths of despair...

10:00.350 --> 10:03.910
And that's why you cut off all
 outside information from the TV and internet.

10:03.910 --> 10:05.500
That's not all.

10:05.500 --> 10:07.780
So as not to cross any kind of case,

10:07.780 --> 10:12.460
I've avoided people and lived as a hermit 
by being a day sleeper. But now...

10:14.100 --> 10:15.670
You went that far just to...

10:15.670 --> 10:20.140
I have a fatal flaw as a detective.

10:20.820 --> 10:22.200
A flaw?

10:22.200 --> 10:25.990
A truly troublesome one.
One that no doctor has been able to fix.

10:25.990 --> 10:28.640
Could it be... Are you sick?

10:28.640 --> 10:29.810
You could say that.

10:32.170 --> 10:36.860
<i>So the reason he confines himself to this
 soft floor is because his body is weak?</i>

10:37.550 --> 10:40.420
<i>He actually wants to be a detective,</i>

10:40.420 --> 10:42.760
<i>but he lives like this because he's sick.</i>

10:43.070 --> 10:44.930
If you get it now, then leave!

10:44.930 --> 10:47.690
If I take sleeping pills to knock me out
for three days, it'll be fine!

10:47.690 --> 10:48.740
No.

10:48.740 --> 10:50.240
I'm taking you with me.

10:51.080 --> 10:52.710
I'll be your support!

10:56.210 --> 10:58.810
Th-Thanks, but I'm not interested
 in the trouble.

10:58.810 --> 11:01.450
Why waste your talents?

11:01.450 --> 11:04.390
What could be more important
than human lives at stake?

11:04.390 --> 11:06.900
Right now, I can't think of anything

11:06.900 --> 11:10.350
that should come before
 stopping a serial killer!

11:10.350 --> 11:12.170
Th-That's not the issue here.

11:12.170 --> 11:13.560
Please trust me.

11:14.060 --> 11:17.280
I promise I'll back you up
 however you need me!

11:23.570 --> 11:24.910
You pure, naïve fool.

11:24.910 --> 11:26.030
Fool?!

11:27.920 --> 11:30.280
So be it. I'll help you.

11:31.550 --> 11:32.170
You mean...

11:32.170 --> 11:32.960
But listen well.

11:33.500 --> 11:35.670
No matter what,
don't take your eyes off me.

11:37.500 --> 11:38.790
You got it.

11:38.790 --> 11:41.460
If you start feeling sick, 
I'll push you in a wheelchair.

11:41.460 --> 11:43.230
What are you talking about?

11:43.230 --> 11:45.040
What do you mean?

11:45.040 --> 11:46.200
Whatever.

11:49.570 --> 11:51.650
We're running all the way 
to the crime scene...

11:51.650 --> 11:53.500
Isshiki Totomaru.

11:53.940 --> 11:58.190
<b>#01   The Case of the Metropolitan Serial Drownings</b>

11:56.190 --> 11:58.190
<b>Kazahana Park</b>

12:03.970 --> 12:05.680
You've sure got stamina...

12:05.680 --> 12:07.660
Have you really been a hermit for years?

12:08.310 --> 12:10.040
Yeah, I have.

12:10.480 --> 12:13.010
I got bored, so I remodeled 
an empty room into a gym.

12:13.010 --> 12:15.250
I train four hours every day.

12:15.250 --> 12:16.470
Are you some kind of athlete?

12:16.470 --> 12:17.870
Detective Isshiki!

12:22.400 --> 12:23.500
This way.

12:26.170 --> 12:29.390
According to the victim's business card, 
he's a private investment broker.

12:29.390 --> 12:32.680
His name's Okamasa, and he had
a ticket for a business party last night.

12:32.680 --> 12:35.400
No one reported seeing him at the event.

12:35.800 --> 12:38.820
Let's see... None of his other 
personal belongings stood out.

12:42.210 --> 12:43.550
Don't mind me.

12:43.550 --> 12:44.730
Hey!

12:43.990 --> 12:45.240
What are you doing?!

12:46.170 --> 12:48.200
I will avenge you.

12:48.200 --> 12:50.660
Kamonohashi-san?

12:50.660 --> 12:52.760
You're a mysterious corpse, aren't you?

12:53.460 --> 12:55.330
Drowning in a place like this...

12:56.540 --> 13:00.780
Why did you hand over your 
valuables without a fight?

13:02.050 --> 13:06.110
Isshiki-san, did you tell him
about how we found the other victims?

13:06.110 --> 13:07.140
No.

13:07.420 --> 13:09.350
Corpses want to talk.

13:11.180 --> 13:15.230
The white froth on his mouth 
indicates the possibility of drowning.

13:15.230 --> 13:18.900
It doesn't look like his clothes are disturbed
or there was any struggle.

13:18.900 --> 13:21.360
This nice suit says
he's doing well for himself.

13:21.900 --> 13:24.570
Based on his tan line,
I can tell his watch was stolen.

13:25.140 --> 13:27.680
And determining his identity
with a business card...

13:27.680 --> 13:31.030
means his wallet, containing his ID,
 was also stolen.

13:31.030 --> 13:32.210
I see.

13:32.210 --> 13:33.500
You're exactly right.

13:34.030 --> 13:36.310
Over the last nine months, 
five people have been killed

13:36.310 --> 13:38.290
at irregular intervals with this exact MO.

13:38.290 --> 13:40.250
All their valuables were stolen.

13:40.250 --> 13:41.730
They had no external injuries.

13:41.730 --> 13:45.070
Testing revealed no alcohol
or drugs in their systems.

13:45.070 --> 13:47.720
And they were all found drowned
in places with no water.

13:47.720 --> 13:50.180
It's like magic. It's unreal!

13:51.680 --> 13:53.150
Any connections between the vics?

13:53.150 --> 13:56.190
Nothing significant other 
than that they were all men.

13:58.520 --> 14:02.210
This map shows where
the five of them were last seen

14:02.210 --> 14:05.010
and where we believe they were all going.

14:05.010 --> 14:09.870
A date, a celebration, a class reunion, 
a wedding, and a birthday party, huh?

14:09.870 --> 14:11.070
All over the place, right?

14:11.070 --> 14:15.120
If you work out the overlap here,
you can narrow down your search area.

14:15.120 --> 14:17.490
That'll be where they all
ran into the culprit.

14:17.490 --> 14:22.290
But there's nowhere in that zone
with enough water to drown in.

14:22.720 --> 14:27.130
Is there even anywhere you can drown
a grown man without him putting up a fight?

14:35.550 --> 14:36.930
There is.

14:37.580 --> 14:38.770
I know a great place for it.

14:38.770 --> 14:39.980
Huh?

14:39.980 --> 14:43.170
Even after a five-year hiatus, 
I haven't gotten rusty at all!

14:43.170 --> 14:43.690
What?

14:44.480 --> 14:47.130
I feel bad for you, but I'm glad to be alive!

14:47.130 --> 14:48.650
I'm so blessed to be detective!

14:49.550 --> 14:50.860
That's so inappropriate!

14:51.470 --> 14:53.920
This is my style.

14:53.920 --> 14:58.470
Treat them with respect and kindness, 
and the dead will open their hearts to you.

14:58.470 --> 15:00.920
Y-You mean that metaphorically, right?

15:04.760 --> 15:06.260
Now, let's be off.

15:06.260 --> 15:07.840
Off? To where?

15:07.840 --> 15:10.300
To arrest the culprit, of course.

15:10.950 --> 15:12.420
You already know who it is?

15:12.420 --> 15:13.010
Yes.

15:13.010 --> 15:16.250
The police investigated for nine months 
and couldn't crack this, you know?

15:16.250 --> 15:18.930
That's why you came to me, isn't it, Toto?

15:18.930 --> 15:22.590
Well, yeah, but...
it's been, like, three minutes.

15:22.590 --> 15:23.690
Wait, huh? "Toto"?

15:23.690 --> 15:26.130
"Totomaru" is just too long.

15:26.130 --> 15:28.400
"A" or "B" would be fine, 
but let's go with "Toto."

15:30.610 --> 15:33.090
First things first, Toto,
take out some cash for me.

15:33.090 --> 15:34.320
What kind of con is this?

15:34.840 --> 15:39.000
Kamo, kamo, kamo, kamo, kamo...

15:39.000 --> 15:41.730
<i>And now he's singing some weird song.</i>

15:41.730 --> 15:43.320
That man seems like bad news.

15:43.320 --> 15:44.920
Y-Yeah.

15:45.290 --> 15:48.130
<i>Should I really be following him?</i>

15:53.690 --> 15:55.320
You look great!

15:55.320 --> 15:57.810
The tacky, expensive get-up really suits you.

15:57.810 --> 16:00.620
Hang on! Why are you making me wear this?

16:00.620 --> 16:01.850
And why am <i>I</i> paying for it?

16:01.850 --> 16:03.070
An undercover investigation.

16:03.070 --> 16:05.150
My usual suit isn't good enough?

16:05.150 --> 16:07.070
Not for dressing up as a wealthy man.

16:07.070 --> 16:10.190
You can't contain your
mediocre police officer aura.

16:11.670 --> 16:15.340
Now, next we have to do something 
about that messy head of hair.

16:15.340 --> 16:16.990
Look in a mirror and say that again!

16:29.640 --> 16:31.130
Let's go with this place.

16:31.130 --> 16:34.720
I've worked two nights in a row, 
so I'm definitely going to fall asleep.

16:34.720 --> 16:35.900
Really?

16:35.900 --> 16:38.470
In this age,
I didn't think any idiot other than me

16:38.470 --> 16:40.770
would go two nights without sleep.

16:40.770 --> 16:42.340
I didn't peg you for the type.

16:42.770 --> 16:44.650
This'll be fun. You should stay awake.

16:44.650 --> 16:46.480
The way you think is so chaotic!

16:46.480 --> 16:51.140
<i>Should I really be doing
what this guy tells me to?</i>

16:51.440 --> 16:53.150
<b>Walk-Ins Very Welcome</b>

16:53.150 --> 16:54.860
Raptor   Academy

16:54.860 --> 16:56.570
Welcome!

16:56.570 --> 16:58.080
H-Hello.

16:58.080 --> 16:59.280
Are you in a hurry?

16:59.280 --> 17:02.440
No. Um, I'm trying to 
change my image a little.

17:02.440 --> 17:04.440
Of course. I totally understand.

17:04.800 --> 17:07.000
Let me take your coat.

17:07.000 --> 17:08.700
Right this way, please.

17:12.190 --> 17:13.480
Wanna come over today?

17:13.480 --> 17:16.380
Drinking black sugar syrup outside 
makes it taste so good!

17:14.040 --> 17:15.830
What? Really? I'd love to!

17:16.380 --> 17:17.630
What was that?

17:17.630 --> 17:19.100
Best to pretend we didn't see anything.

17:21.110 --> 17:24.050
Really? So you're good with stocks, are you?

17:24.050 --> 17:25.730
That's impressive.

17:26.050 --> 17:29.250
Now, we'll start with a shampoo. 
Come up to the basin.

17:29.250 --> 17:30.350
All right.

17:43.040 --> 17:44.270
Sir?

18:09.520 --> 18:11.080
That's as far as you go...

18:16.870 --> 18:20.320
Mr. Killer Barber.

18:20.720 --> 18:21.780
What?!

18:22.080 --> 18:23.490
H-How did you...

18:24.270 --> 18:26.580
Opening locks is a special interest of mine.

18:32.790 --> 18:34.380
What?! This can't be!

18:34.380 --> 18:35.630
What's going on?

18:35.630 --> 18:38.770
I held my breath for a minute 
during the shampoo like you said,

18:38.770 --> 18:40.260
so I couldn't say anything.

18:40.580 --> 18:42.220
But what on earth is going on here?!

18:43.130 --> 18:47.890
You were about to be murdered
in a way only a barber could pull off.

18:47.890 --> 18:49.060
What?

18:49.060 --> 18:52.790
How is it that none of the victims
showed drugs in their systems,

18:52.790 --> 18:55.280
yet not a one of them put up a fight?

18:55.280 --> 18:58.350
The secret lies in that shampoo station.

18:59.030 --> 19:01.240
The shampoo station was filled...

19:01.240 --> 19:02.950
with oxygen-deficient air.

19:02.950 --> 19:04.660
Oxygen-deficient air?

19:04.660 --> 19:09.210
Air with an oxygen saturation below 18.

19:09.210 --> 19:14.370
If a person takes a single breath of air 
when it's less than 10, they faint.

19:14.370 --> 19:19.350
Pouring hot water over dry ice to generate 
carbon dioxide would accomplish that.

19:19.350 --> 19:23.790
S-So if I had breathed that in,
then the water filling the basin would've...

19:23.790 --> 19:25.390
You'd have drowned.

19:27.100 --> 19:29.190
But how did you know it was a barber?

19:29.190 --> 19:30.560
Why this shop?

19:30.560 --> 19:33.390
The victims were all men
whose hair was growing out.

19:33.390 --> 19:36.140
Many of them were showing 
undyed roots at their hairlines.

19:36.140 --> 19:39.150
So if they all had big events lined up
like parties and reunions

19:39.150 --> 19:43.030
that they'd naturally want to look good for,
it only makes sense

19:43.410 --> 19:45.740
to hit up a salon or a barber, right?

19:46.390 --> 19:48.580
And given the oxygen-deficient air trick,

19:48.580 --> 19:51.740
the head-first shampooing station
at a barber's is likely bet.

19:51.740 --> 19:54.750
From those clues, I figured it'd be
a shop targeting new customers,

19:54.750 --> 19:57.670
so I focused on places in the 
victims' overlapping areas of movement

19:57.670 --> 19:59.150
that accepted walk-ins.

19:57.670 --> 19:59.630
<b>Walk-Ins Very Welcome</b>

19:59.630 --> 20:01.130
The scene of the crime also had to be

20:01.130 --> 20:03.340
somewhere people couldn't 
see in from the outside

20:03.810 --> 20:06.750
and somewhere you could get
dry ice nearby.

20:06.750 --> 20:08.440
This place fit all the criteria.

20:08.440 --> 20:12.610
I see. But what if the victims had told 
people they were going to a barber?

20:12.610 --> 20:15.460
The profession lends itself
to chatting up clients.

20:15.460 --> 20:18.270
Whether a customer lives alone,
if they had plans to come...

20:18.650 --> 20:21.240
A barber could learn that all
straight from the horse's mouth.

20:22.860 --> 20:26.650
To use that against the culprit, 
I had you dress in expensive clothes

20:26.650 --> 20:28.580
and tell a story about hitting it big in stocks.

20:28.580 --> 20:32.850
I made you play exactly the kind of
wealthy walk-in our culprit prefers.

20:32.850 --> 20:35.220
He bought it hook, line, and sinker.

20:36.360 --> 20:38.830
Every detail of the trick 
being put into practice

20:38.830 --> 20:41.510
was recorded on Detective Isshiki's phone.

20:41.510 --> 20:43.970
You're cops? Crap!

20:48.290 --> 20:49.340
Stop!

20:57.210 --> 20:59.150
I went ahead and locked it.

20:59.150 --> 21:00.900
Stop resisting! It's no use!

21:01.380 --> 21:03.160
Damn it!

21:04.790 --> 21:06.430
Why did you kill six people?

21:06.430 --> 21:08.620
What? You want to know why?

21:08.620 --> 21:11.840
Money! It was the money. What else?

21:12.230 --> 21:15.460
Y-You'd really kill six 
people just for the money?

21:15.460 --> 21:18.850
It was so easy. 
And I don't feel the least bit guilty.

21:19.200 --> 21:21.350
Rich people preyed on me first.

21:21.350 --> 21:22.670
The debt I'm in from stocks...

21:22.670 --> 21:24.630
Do you have any idea what they've done to me?!

21:24.630 --> 21:25.820
Stocks?

21:26.170 --> 21:28.090
This is all over a simple grudge?

21:28.090 --> 21:29.460
That was the reason you—

21:29.460 --> 21:30.840
Shut up!

21:30.840 --> 21:33.560
You have no idea what it's like
 to be someone pressured every day to—

21:32.350 --> 21:33.560
Jump.

21:33.560 --> 21:34.270
Huh?

21:34.770 --> 21:36.410
Jump from here.

21:36.410 --> 21:37.580
What?

21:37.580 --> 21:39.730
Someone who devalues the lives of others

21:40.200 --> 21:42.620
has no right to keep living in this world.

21:45.030 --> 21:46.950
Hey! What are you on about?

21:46.950 --> 21:47.820
Jump.

21:47.820 --> 21:49.680
I thought you just wanted
to solve the mystery!

21:49.680 --> 21:50.620
Jump?

21:53.540 --> 21:54.350
Yes...

21:54.350 --> 21:56.120
Okay, now you're following
instructions <i>too</i> well!

21:56.530 --> 21:59.830
You might be joking around,
but there're folks who'll take you seriously.

21:59.830 --> 22:01.880
Jump from here...

22:02.300 --> 22:04.540
Pressuring him so irresponsibly is just...

22:07.510 --> 22:08.720
You've gotta be kidding me!

22:17.730 --> 22:19.150
What did I do?

22:19.150 --> 22:20.750
Toto, where's the culprit?

22:20.750 --> 22:23.610
He just jumped because of you!

22:25.140 --> 22:27.290
I've done it again...

22:27.290 --> 22:31.020
I should've stuck to my guns.
I never should've trusted anyone else.

22:31.350 --> 22:32.950
I have no right to be a detect—

22:32.950 --> 22:35.420
Stop muttering and give me a hand!

22:39.390 --> 22:41.240
Help me!

22:41.240 --> 22:43.130
The culprit is alive?

22:43.530 --> 22:45.560
Did you save him?

22:45.560 --> 22:47.370
You can see that, can't you?!

22:47.370 --> 22:50.940
Can he be saved by such a foolish detective?

22:50.940 --> 22:54.180
Without any hesitation whatsoever,
he put his own life on the line to...

22:54.510 --> 22:56.020
No, it's the opposite!

22:56.020 --> 22:58.070
He's a pure, naïve fool!

22:58.070 --> 23:00.420
His body reacts before reason kicks in!

23:00.420 --> 23:03.310
Hey! Stop dissing me and help!

23:03.670 --> 23:06.280
Kamonohashi... Hey, Ron!

23:13.190 --> 23:14.700
In the style of a bungee jump.

23:14.700 --> 23:15.730
Look at that!

23:15.730 --> 23:17.200
There are people dangling up there!

23:18.300 --> 23:19.760
I've changed my mind!

23:19.760 --> 23:22.060
I feel infinite possibilities here, Toto!

23:22.060 --> 23:22.630
What?!

23:22.630 --> 23:25.100
Thanks to you, I've had a brilliant idea!

23:25.100 --> 23:25.810
What?

23:25.810 --> 23:26.750
This is terrible!

23:26.750 --> 23:28.210
Someone call the police!

23:27.070 --> 23:29.600
Just hurry and pull me up, please!

23:29.600 --> 23:31.270
Ron!

23:34.830 --> 23:35.640
What?!

23:36.110 --> 23:39.600
You never told me that your "flaw"
is a sickness where you kill the culprit!

23:39.600 --> 23:42.100
I have no conscious memory of doing so.

23:42.100 --> 23:44.540
Apparently, I always pressure 
the culprits to death.

23:44.540 --> 23:46.920
When I come back to my senses, 
it's too late.

23:46.920 --> 23:50.530
That's why my solved case rate is 100 percent,

23:50.530 --> 23:53.240
but my arrest rate is 0 percent.

23:53.240 --> 23:55.450
That's awful! That's just too terrible!

23:55.450 --> 23:57.670
That's why I was forbidden 
to act as a detective

23:57.670 --> 23:59.180
and why I cut myself off from cases.

23:59.180 --> 24:00.590
Good call!

24:00.590 --> 24:05.170
But at last, you've broken
my disgraceful streak.

24:05.930 --> 24:09.150
The mystery of why Kiku sent you to me...

24:09.150 --> 24:11.200
This has to be the answer.

24:11.200 --> 24:11.880
What?

24:11.880 --> 24:15.070
I don't need some
brilliant partner at my side.

24:15.070 --> 24:16.600
I need a pure, naïve fool.

24:16.600 --> 24:19.020
And that fool is me?

24:19.020 --> 24:19.930
I'm your partner?

24:21.670 --> 24:23.790
Every case you stumble upon...

24:23.790 --> 24:25.100
Bring them all to me.

24:27.030 --> 24:28.560
Don't worry.

24:28.560 --> 24:30.780
I'll assume responsibility 
for that brain of yours.

24:30.780 --> 24:32.990
You follow, Toto?

24:33.750 --> 24:36.450
Starting today, you are a great detective!
